PATCH 644: restore actual device tail dispatch and DSP reset (board:0003/0026).

Source receipt tools/oracle/device_reset_case.json proves the actual77fa CALL
into23c4, byte MOV/CMP, DWORD dispatch table and tail JMP to133a. Original
modes1..4 select133a; mode0 selects the existing bare RET at2294. The out-of-
range branch is XOR EAX,EAX/RET. Dispatch creates no additional guest frame.

133a preserves all untouched full GP/segment/control fields, uses WORD DX and
BYTE AL, CLI/STI, actual20/8000 loop immediates and device-driven LOOPE. It
performs every original fetch and actual shared I/O; no poll count, AA sample,
success result or aggregate elapsed time is supplied. Both real return paths
consume the original DWORD caller frame. The shared CPU context carries raw
and lazy flags. Normal-core exits in the existing clock materialize flags,
including the reset event's requeue and natural polling-budget exhaustion.

The reaching regression calls both new sorted map entries and compares all
225 dispatch/219 direct original fetch states, complete GP/segments/raw-lazy
flags/control/CPU budgets and all16MiB isolated memory. Parent entries are
absent on both targets. Original mode1 source is the dynamic proof; alternate
modes/error-AA branches require independent reaching coverage. Production
77e2/op6c, effects/op68, protected IRQ/IRET/IF transport, final mixed PCM and
complete original frame/audio parity remain open. No legacy C-only caller is
assigned guessed full registers or raw flags.
